## Add pending-action request/confirm/cancel routes

Context: Task 4 of Graph Chat MCP alignment adds the Action confirmation
flow so Graph Chat can propose a Unity Catalog function call without ever
auto-invoking it — a one-time token gates the actual invocation behind an
explicit UI confirm click.

Changes:

1. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   Add `POST /dtwin/nodes/action/request` (validates entity + allow-listed
   action, mints a session-bound single-use token, no invoke),
   `POST /dtwin/nodes/action/confirm` (consumes the token, marks it used
   before invoking so a double-click can't double-invoke, calls
   `NodeContextService.invoke_action` once), and
   `POST /dtwin/nodes/action/cancel` (best-effort discard, always 200).
   Extend the Graph Chat session cache with `pending_actions` keyed by
   token (`domain`, `entity_uri`, `action_full_name`, `expires_at`,
   `used`), a 120s TTL (`_PENDING_ACTION_TTL_SEC`), and a
   `_pending_actions_prune` helper so expired tokens don't accumulate.
2. `tests/units/api/test_dtwin_nodes_action_confirm.py`
   TDD coverage: mint-without-invoke, confirm-invokes-once-then-rejects-
   reuse, unknown action / unmatched entity rejection, missing/unknown/
   expired/domain-mismatched token rejection, and cancel discarding a
   token before it can be confirmed.

