## Document single-process assumption for pending actions

Context: Code review (Task 4) flagged that double-invoke protection and
pending-action tokens rely on in-memory per-process session cache; scaling
Uvicorn workers would silently break unless documented.

Changes:

1. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   Comment near `_PENDING_ACTION_TTL_SEC` noting per-process cache, single-
   worker / one-event-loop assumption, and need for sticky sessions or shared
   state when scaling workers.

