## Wire Graph Chat tools to session-aware node context and pending-action routes

Context: Task 5 of Graph Chat MCP alignment enriches the existing
`agent_dtwin_chat` tools with per-class Actions metadata and adds the two
tools the LLM needs to inspect and propose Actions on a node, mirroring the
MCP server's `get_entity_context` (but deliberately NOT porting
`invoke_entity_action` — invocation stays gated behind UI confirmation via
`request_entity_action`, handled by Task 6/7).

Changes:

1. `src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/tools.py`
   Add `_get_class_actions` (GET `/dtwin/classes`, cached on
   `ctx.dtwin_class_actions`) and the `_ACTION_HINT` constant. Enrich
   `tool_list_entity_types` with per-type dataset/action lines (same text
   style as the MCP server) and `tool_describe_entity` with
   `class_actions=`/`action_invoke_hint=` via `format_find_response`. Add
   `tool_get_entity_context` (GET `/dtwin/nodes/context`, forwards
   `fetch_dataset_rows`/`dataset_row_limit`/`follow_bridges`, formats via
   `format_node_context_response`) and `tool_request_entity_action` (POST
   `/dtwin/nodes/action/request`, sets `ctx.pending_action` on success and
   returns a short message telling the model the UI will render a
   confirmation card). Register both in `TOOL_DEFINITIONS`/`TOOL_HANDLERS`.
2. `tests/units/agents/test_agent_dtwin_chat.py`
   TDD coverage: `list_entity_types` dataset/action enrichment,
   `describe_entity` class-actions enrichment, `get_entity_context`
   flag-forwarding/validation/HTTP-error paths, `request_entity_action`
   pending-token capture, missing-args guard, and backend-failure /
   HTTP-error paths that leave `ctx.pending_action` unset.

